ZEsarPCW embedded/libretro data:

-Native PCW bootstrap
libretro/pcw_boot.c implements the documented PCW 8256/8512 disk bootstrap
interface in C. It is original ZEsarPCW port work under GPLv3, copyright
(c) 2026 retrodiv <retrodiv@proton.me>. No Amstrad firmware is included.
See docs/BOOTSTRAP.md for its functional basis and compatibility boundary.

-OpenPCW-OS fallback environment and helper disc
The standalone OpenPCW-OS project builds openpcw_os.dsk from its
MIT-licensed assembly sources. Its source identity and release hashes are
recorded in sources/openpcw-os/. The disk is embedded as a C array alongside
the documented shell-ready address used for the media handoff.
The display font derives from Microsoft's MIT-licensed MS-DOS 4.0 source.
Preserve sources/openpcw-os/LICENSES.txt, which includes both upstream notices.
The generator and C templates are port work under GPLv3; they do not change
the MIT terms of the disk contents or integration metadata.

-Floppy-drive sound samples
Bundled as PCM arrays in libretro/pcw_fdc_samples.h. The header credits the
samples to the PituKa / wiituka Amstrad CPC emulator by David Colmenero
(D_Skywalk), distributed under GNU GPL v2 or later, using version 3 here.
The editable WAV sources and generator are included under sources/fdc/.

